        {
            "content_html": "<img src=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23019147?u=4c0de81596ced64dc067dea5686f7ca2912db0cb&v=4\" width=\"64\" height=\"64\" alt=\"\"/><br/><h3 dir=\"auto\">Description</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">This PR:</p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Changes the phrasing to follow this approach: \"matches {what} when a user {action}\".</li>\n<li>Removes \"but does not necessarily activate it\" because it's not very clear and can cause confusion. This idea is also being explained in the next sentence.</li>\n<li>spells out \"activate\" as \"pressing the mouse button\" in the second sentence.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">Motivation</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">I came across this page randomly and noticed a scope to improve for clarity.</p>",
